Three specific bugs across expenseParser.ts, Editor.tsx, and index.css are causing these issues:

Checklist Total (parseChecklistExpenses in src/utils/expenseParser.ts):

Leading digits were being stripped: The cleanup regex /^[☑☐✓\-\*\d\.\s\+]+/ included \d, which erased the amount at the start of lines like "20₹ - Local up" (turning it into "₹ - Local up" and returning a 0 total).

Detached DOM innerText collapsed all lines into one: Because tempDiv was never attached to the document, tempDiv.innerText fell back to textContent with no \n line breaks between <div>, <p>, or .todo-line elements—concatenating all expenses into a single line.

Table rows & SUM footer were double-counted: Once a table was inserted, parseChecklistExpenses also parsed the table's own rows and SUM ₹... footer.

Stale Banner state: ChecklistExpenseBanner was passed card.body, which only updated after the debounce instead of live on input.

Table Sum & Row Navigation (recalculateNotionTables & handleBodyKeyDown in src/components/Editor.tsx):

Dot stripping bug in recalculateNotionTables: .replace(/[^0-9\.]/g, '') kept periods from text like "Rs. 20", turning it into ".20" (₹0.20), and merged multiline numbers like "20\n30" into "2030".

Pressing Enter in a table cell: Pressing Enter inside a <td> inserted a <div>/<br> inside the cell instead of moving to the next row or adding a new row.

Enter Key with /todo (Editor.tsx & src/index.css):

Collapsed 0px height on empty .todo-content: .todo-line uses align-items: flex-start, so an empty <span class="todo-content"> with no <br> or min-height collapsed to 0px height, causing Chrome to drop focus/selection immediately after pressing Enter.

Slash menu stayed open after /: checkSlashTrigger only closed the menu if !beforeCaret.includes('/'), keeping showSlashMenu true on lines containing a / and hijacking subsequent Enter presses.

bodyRef.current?.focus() stole focus: Calling bodyRef.current?.focus() in applySlashAction right before insertTodoLine prevented focus from landing inside the nested contenteditable="true" .todo-content span.

